1.1 Two Pointers - Opposite ends

idea - Place one pointer say Left at the start of the Array and place another pointer at the end of the Array. Move both the pointer towards each other untill Left<Right.

example: Two Sum - Given a target value and a sorted array, find the two numbers where the sum equals the target value

int left=0;
int right = arr.length-1;

while(left<right){
  if(arr[left]+arr[right]==target){
    return new int[] {left,right}
  }else if(arr[left]+arr[right]>target){
    end=end-1;
  }else{
    start=start+1
  }
}
return new int[] {-1,-1}

