1.2 two Pointers - Same Direction

idea - Place one pointer ats start and another pointer at either start or start+1 and the last pointer is used for scan and first pointer is used to rewrite

example: Move duplicates to the last position of Array an return upto distinct numbers in the Array.

int left=0;   // declaring and initializing the left pointer at the start of the array
for(int right=1;right<arr.length;right++){ // second pointer is placed at 1st index and the index is moving towards end of the array
  if(arr[left]!=arr[right]){ // whenever left == right , then right moves 1 index to right, if left != right then that means a new distinct element is found then it should be swapped with
    left++;                  // left +1 element becuase left is already a distinct element
    swap(arr,left,right);
  }
}
return left+1;  


example : Move the target number to last place of the array

int left = 0;
for(int right=0;right<arr.length;right++){ // using right=0 bcoz the target number could also be the first element, right=0 makes a check for first element
  if(arr[right]!=target){ // whenever arr[right]!=target, then that means if should be swapped with left element which either be in the right position if there is no target value present
    swap(arr,left,right); // till the right index and once there is a target value in the middle, left ++ is going to get skipped and left contains the target position annd it is swapped 
    left++;               // with right so that it moves to the last index.
  }
}

return left;











